He was gonna leave his wife.

00:35:04.580 --> 00:35:05.980
I feel so stupid.

00:35:06.630 --> 00:35:07.070
Don't.

00:35:08.030 --> 00:35:09.730
You did something most people can't.

00:35:10.570 --> 00:35:12.890
You put aside your fear and let your heart come first.

00:35:14.360 --> 00:35:16.160
That's pretty damn admirable if you ask me.

00:35:18.100 --> 00:35:18.740
I guess so.

00:35:20.650 --> 00:35:21.450
You're a good listener.

00:35:22.740 --> 00:35:24.420
That sister of yours is lucky to have you.

00:35:26.450 --> 00:35:26.890
Not really.

00:35:29.700 --> 00:35:29.980
I know what's...

00:35:30.000 --> 00:35:35.360
park, but can we talk more about that trip to the Bahamas? Sure. How do Pulaski usually pay for

00:35:35.360 --> 00:35:40.910
things? Credit cards? Pete doesn't believe in credit. He'd throw hundreds around like it was

00:35:40.910 --> 00:35:46.860
nothing. He even left me with a stack of them when he skipped off to Aruba. Wait, he left the Bahamas

00:35:46.860 --> 00:35:52.530
and went to Aruba? Yeah, he said he had some business with a bank. What a crock. I know he had a girl

00:35:52.530 --> 00:35:59.670
stashed over there. Not a girl, Summer. Those teachers' pensions. Get this!

00:36:00.090 --> 00:36:02.050
I just talked with a source of Chicago National Bank

00:36:02.050 --> 00:36:03.590
that says Pulaski wired $3 million

00:36:03.590 --> 00:36:04.990
into an offshore account in Aruba.

00:36:05.450 --> 00:36:06.690
Summer says he's flying there tonight.

00:36:06.870 --> 00:36:09.150
We have to get to his place and catch him before he leaves.

00:36:09.510 --> 00:36:12.070
Are you listening to me, Babcock?

00:36:13.870 --> 00:36:14.590
I'm not doing it.

00:36:15.720 --> 00:36:17.830
Look, I'm sorry about what I said,

00:36:17.910 --> 00:36:19.450
but you can't make this personal now.

00:36:19.690 --> 00:36:21.230
I'm not doing it. You are.

00:36:22.860 --> 00:36:25.000
Take the crew, I'll handle Jack, and alert the authorities.

00:36:25.300 --> 00:36:26.980
Why are you doing this?

00:36:27.140 --> 00:36:28.080
Because you're good, Dennis.

00:36:28.360 --> 00:36:29.740
Because you never gave up on that lead.

00:36:30.410 --> 00:36:34.760
And because maybe, just maybe, I'm not the shallow jerk you've taken before.

00:36:35.120 --> 00:36:38.180
Oh, look, you gotta go. Go.

00:36:38.910 --> 00:36:39.270
Taxi!

00:36:39.550 --> 00:36:45.420
I come to. I want to watch that bastard eat it.

00:36:45.780 --> 00:36:46.040
Uh-huh.

00:36:46.180 --> 00:36:49.920
You guys make a good team.

00:37:08.800 --> 00:37:10.420
Come on, what's the hold-up?

00:37:12.690 --> 00:37:13.930
Sorry to keep you waiting, Councilman.

00:37:15.070 --> 00:37:15.990
Got a minute to chat?

00:37:28.310 --> 00:37:29.980
I'm Pepper Dennis, live from...

00:37:30.890 --> 00:37:34.290
where a local politician has some explaining to do.

00:37:34.880 --> 00:37:38.140
Summer Waters, an ex-girlfriend of Pulaski's, broke the story.

00:37:38.440 --> 00:37:41.480
He betrayed my trust, just like he betrayed Chicago.

00:37:42.260 --> 00:37:43.620
That's impotence for you.

00:37:44.520 --> 00:37:49.040
Currently, there's no word on how Pulaski was able to embezzle the funds undetected.

00:37:49.260 --> 00:37:50.640
This just in from City Hall.

00:37:50.900 --> 00:37:52.680
Pulaski has outed three accomplices,

00:37:52.780 --> 00:37:55.060
including someone in the city treasurer's office

00:37:55.060 --> 00:37:57.780
who agreed to cook the books in exchange for a share of the money.

00:37:58.170 --> 00:37:59.690
An arraignment is scheduled for tomorrow.

00:38:00.120 --> 00:38:03.220
Until then, Pulaski will have to trade a Caribbean life of leisure

00:38:03.220 --> 00:38:05.360
for a cot in the Cook County Jail.

00:38:05.580 --> 00:38:08.260
For WEIE News, I'm Pepper Dennis.

00:38:08.980 --> 00:38:10.280
And I'm Charlie Babcock.

00:38:10.680 --> 00:38:10.960
Good night.

00:38:12.180 --> 00:38:15.380
All right, the numbers are in, and it's good news, folks.

00:38:15.800 --> 00:38:17.100
Chicago likes our new anchor.

00:38:17.340 --> 00:38:18.620
Welcome aboard, Babcock.

00:38:21.770 --> 00:38:24.990
But the real hero of the day is Pepper Dennis,

00:38:25.810 --> 00:38:27.070
WEIE's number one reporter.

00:38:27.440 --> 00:38:29.540
Stubborn kid. Paid off tonight.

00:38:31.120 --> 00:38:32.480
Screw the FCC. You're back.

00:38:37.260 --> 00:38:38.440
Anything you'd like to say?

00:38:39.910 --> 00:38:40.990
Let's watch it again.

00:38:41.600 --> 00:38:42.180
Roll it, Billy!

00:38:49.860 --> 00:38:50.840
Celebration's for you, you know.

00:38:51.560 --> 00:38:53.000
Yeah, I'm not in the mood.

00:38:53.460 --> 00:38:55.840
You're gonna have to get used to sharing applause with the guy.

00:38:56.500 --> 00:38:57.060
He's good.

00:38:57.790 --> 00:38:59.980
I know. He did s***.

00:39:00.000 --> 00:39:01.660
something for me today he didn't have to do.

00:39:01.840 --> 00:39:05.940
He gave me a chance. Wonder why you won't give him

00:39:05.940 --> 00:39:08.390
one. Well, you know I can't do that,

00:39:08.470 --> 00:39:10.300
can he? Pepper, everyone here

00:39:10.300 --> 00:39:12.440
loves you. Why wouldn't they want you to be happy?

00:39:13.500 --> 00:39:15.040
Okay, tell me what you want

00:39:15.040 --> 00:39:22.000
and be specific. This doesn't have to

00:39:22.000 --> 00:39:24.350
wait anymore. So what are you gonna do about it?

00:39:24.570 --> 00:39:26.270
Nothing. I've been horrible to him.

00:39:27.300 --> 00:39:28.980
Well, I guess that's it then.

00:39:30.000 --> 00:39:32.560
I mean, that is you after all.

00:39:33.710 --> 00:39:36.850
Unmotivated, a quitter, never up for a challenge.

00:39:37.980 --> 00:39:38.980
He just headed for the elevator.

00:40:10.300 --> 00:40:12.840
Hey Dennis, you want something?

00:40:21.270 --> 00:40:21.590
Sure?

00:40:22.700 --> 00:40:23.200
Nothing.

00:41:14.520 --> 00:41:16.400
get this mess cleaned up before you got home.

00:41:18.090 --> 00:41:22.200
Yeah, sure, just get out of your way.

00:41:24.360 --> 00:41:24.660
Stay.

00:41:31.180 --> 00:41:35.520
I want you to stay, and I want you to take the job at the station.

00:41:36.950 --> 00:41:38.730
At least until you figure out what to do next.

00:41:40.480 --> 00:41:43.140
What about me getting in the way of your plans?

00:41:44.810 --> 00:41:47.140
Yeah, well, plans change.

00:41:48.930 --> 00:41:49.690
You're dull on me.

00:41:53.400 --> 00:41:54.020
Okay, I'll stay.

00:41:56.260 --> 00:41:56.820
One condition.

00:41:57.160 --> 00:41:57.860
The name's Pepper.

00:41:58.390 --> 00:41:58.950
Oh, Patty.

00:41:59.720 --> 00:41:59.900
Bye.

00:42:01.980 --> 00:42:07.280
A little better, stay a little gray

00:42:07.600 --> 00:42:09.080
Live it up, live it long

00:42:09.080 --> 00:42:12.160
You can always count on those unexpected moments

00:42:12.160 --> 00:42:14.460
When the pleasure's just sweet
